<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 4 December, from 771 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">771 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,255 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Carloman dies, leaving Charlemagne sole king of the Franks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carloman-i">Carloman I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s brother and co-ruler, died suddenly. Charlemagne took over his kingdom, and Carloman's widow fled with her sons to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carloman-i">Carloman I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1259">1259 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">767 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IX and Henry III make peace in the Treaty of Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1259">Treaty of Paris</a>, by which Henry gave up his claims to Normandy, Anjou, Maine and Poitou and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> as a duchy, paying homage for it to the French king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1259">Treaty of Paris (1259)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1370">1370 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">656 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bertrand du Guesclin's French army defeats the English at Pontvallain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In two separate engagements, a French army of 5,200 men under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin">Bertrand du Guesclin</a> heavily defeated an English force of about the same size, which had broken away from the army of Sir Robert Knolles after a dispute between the commanders.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1563">1563 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">463 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Trent holds its final session</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a>, which had opened on 13 December 1545, held its final session. Called in response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, it had reaffirmed Catholic doctrine on scripture, justification and the seven sacraments and ordered reforms such as seminaries for priests.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Observer is first published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first issue of The Observer appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. It is the world's oldest Sunday newspaper still in publication.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1867">1867 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The National Grange is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Oliver Kelley and colleagues founded the Order of Patrons of Husbandry, known as the Grange, in Washington. It became a powerful voice for farmers against railway rates and monopolies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mary Celeste is found drifting and abandoned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crew of the Dei Gratia found the American brigantine Mary Celeste sailing unmanned in the Atlantic, her cargo intact and lifeboat gone. The fate of the ten people aboard has never been explained.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pan Am ceases operations</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pan American World Airways flew its last flight after 64 years. The airline had pioneered transoceanic air travel and launched the Boeing 747, but it never recovered from deregulation, recession and the Lockerbie bombing.</p></div></li></ol>
